meta {
  name: 31 Update Content Sections
  type: http
  seq: 31
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/lab-reports/{{labReportId}}/content-sections
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "usefulFor": "Screening for kidney function.",
    "interpretation": "Elevated values may indicate impaired renal function.",
    "limitations": "Not valid in hemolyzed samples.",
    "remarks": "Repeat if result is borderline.",
    "references": "Tietz Textbook of Clinical Chemistry, 6th Ed."
  }
}

docs {
  Persist a technician's edit to one or more of the Test Entry screen's 5
  Notes sections (LABORATORY.docx §4.5): `usefulFor`, `interpretation`,
  `limitations`, `remarks`, `references`. All 5 fields are optional in the
  body — send only the ones you're changing, or all 5 unconditionally (a
  field whose branch toggle is off is silently ignored, not rejected).

  Each field is a PER-REPORT override, stored on THIS `LabReport` row only.
  It never writes to the shared `LabTest` master (Master Data > Add Test >
  Notes) — editing here affects only this one patient's report, not every
  other order of the same test.

  Editability is gated per field by the branch's TechnicianSetting toggles
  (`isUsefulForEditable` / `isInterpretationEditable` / `isLimitationsEditable`
  / `isRemarksEditable` / `isReferencesEditable`), all default `false`. See
  "Technician Settings" module to enable them.

  Response is the same shape `GET /lab-reports/:id`'s `contentSections`
  returns — each field is this report's just-saved override (if its toggle
  allowed the write) falling back to the `LabTest` master's default
  otherwise.

  Values may be rich-text HTML (Master Data's Notes editor produces HTML) —
  `@MaxLength(20000)` per field to accommodate markup, not just plain text.

  404 `LAB_REPORT_NOT_FOUND` if missing/other-tenant/other-branch. 409
  `LAB_REPORT_LOCKED` if the report is locked.
}
